      {
        "criterion": "Visual material separation",
        "sourceWitness": "BRIEF asks for light matte woven shirt with small soft-crisp folds, smoother matte trouser fold language, and canvas upper versus flat sole separation.",
        "candidateWitness": "The sage shirt shows a fine crosshatched/slub-like weave and shallow crisp creases, enlarged in the portrait. The sand trousers have longer softer vertical folds/creases and a quieter fine surface. The darker navy shoe uppers, pale crossing laces and smooth light sole bands remain distinct.",
        "explanation": "Surface scale, folds, palette and shoe-edge contrast separate the visible clothing roles at plate scale. The trousers retain some woven texture; they read smoother in fold/surface language than the shirt, not as physically different measured materials. No textile process, thickness, opacity or fabric optics is qualified."
      },
      {
        "criterion": "Coherent views and declared framing",
        "sourceWitness": "BRIEF requests complete front and three-quarter clothed figures plus a larger whole-head portrait. Ordinary far-side overlap and intentional portrait chest cropping are allowed; head/hair cropping is not.",
        "candidateWitness": "The left figure reads front. The middle figure uses a modest oblique stance, more strongly turned head and obliquely shown shoe sides; its torso is less turned than its head. Both have whole hair/head boundaries, both hands and every visible shoe inside frame, with space above hair and below soles. The right portrait has its full bob/crown/head inside the image, and intentionally crops shoulders/chest. Garment palette, collar, placket/hem, trouser lengths and shoe design remain coherent across visible views.",
